[{"kind":"noun","hangul":"운동","english":"exercise","topic":"daily-life","chapterIds":["chapter-05","chapter-08"],"grammarIds":["grammar-particle-eul-reul","grammar-ending-want"],"usage":[["운동을 해요","I exercise","object marker 을"],["운동이 재미있어요","exercise is fun","subject marker 이"],["운동을 하고 싶어요","I want to exercise","고 싶어요 want"],["운동을 좋아해요","I like exercise","좋아해요 means like"]],"examples":[["저는 매일 아침에 운동을 해요.","I exercise every morning.","daily habit"],["요즘 운동을 하고 싶어요.","I want to exercise these days.","expressing desire"],["운동이 정말 재미있어요.","Exercise is really fun.","opinion"]],"nuance":"운동 means exercise in general and pairs with 해요 to say work out. The same word can also mean sports or a movement campaign.","mistakes":["Using 만들어요 instead of 해요 with 운동"]},
{"kind":"noun","hangul":"영화","english":"movie","topic":"daily-life","chapterIds":["chapter-05","chapter-08"],"grammarIds":["grammar-particle-eul-reul","grammar-ending-want"],"usage":[["영화를 봐요","I watch a movie","봐요 means watch"],["영화가 재미있어요","the movie is fun","subject marker 가"],["영화를 보고 싶어요","I want to watch a movie","고 싶어요 want"],["영화 한 편","one movie","counter 편"]],"examples":[["주말에 영화를 봐요.","I watch a movie on the weekend.","weekend plan"],["이 영화가 정말 재미있어요.","This movie is really fun.","opinion"],["같이 영화를 보고 싶어요.","I want to watch a movie together.","invitation"]],"nuance":"영화 takes 봐요 (watch), not 들어요 (listen), and a single film is counted with 편. A movie theater is called 영화관.","mistakes":["Using 들어요 instead of 봐요 with 영화"]},
{"kind":"noun","hangul":"음악","english":"music","topic":"daily-life","chapterIds":["chapter-05","chapter-08"],"grammarIds":["grammar-particle-eul-reul","grammar-particle-i-ga"],"usage":[["음악을 들어요","I listen to music","들어요 means listen"],["음악이 좋아요","the music is good","subject marker 이"],["음악을 좋아해요","I like music","좋아해요 means like"],["음악을 틀어요","I play music","틀어요 means play"]],"examples":[["저는 운동할 때 음악을 들어요.","I listen to music when I exercise.","daily habit"],["이 음악이 정말 좋아요.","This music is really good.","opinion"],["저는 조용한 음악을 좋아해요.","I like quiet music.","preference"]],"nuance":"음악 takes 들어요 (listen) because you receive sound, while playing a song is 틀어요. The word covers all kinds of music in general.","mistakes":["Using 봐요 instead of 들어요 with 음악"]},
{"kind":"noun","hangul":"노래","english":"song","topic":"daily-life","chapterIds":["chapter-05","chapter-08"],"grammarIds":["grammar-particle-eul-reul","grammar-ending-can"],"usage":[["노래를 해요","I sing","노래해요 means sing"],["노래를 들어요","I listen to a song","들어요 means listen"],["노래를 할 수 있어요","I can sing","ㄹ 수 있어요 can"],["노래 한 곡","one song","counter 곡"]],"examples":[["저는 노래를 잘 해요.","I sing well.","ability"],["이 노래를 들어요.","I listen to this song.","action"],["저는 한국 노래를 할 수 있어요.","I can sing a Korean song.","expressing ability"]],"nuance":"노래 with 해요 means to sing, while 노래방 is a karaoke room where Koreans love to sing. A single song is counted with 곡.","mistakes":["Saying 노래를 불러요 wrongly as 노래를 말해요"]},
{"kind":"noun","hangul":"춤","english":"dance","topic":"daily-life","chapterIds":["chapter-05","chapter-08"],"grammarIds":["grammar-particle-eul-reul","grammar-ending-can"],"usage":[["춤을 춰요","I dance","춤춰요 means dance"],["춤이 멋있어요","the dance is cool","subject marker 이"],["춤을 출 수 있어요","I can dance","ㄹ 수 있어요 can"],["춤을 배워요","I learn to dance","배워요 means learn"]],"examples":[["저는 춤을 춰요.","I dance.","action"],["그 사람 춤이 정말 멋있어요.","That person dances really well.","opinion"],["저는 춤을 출 수 있어요.","I can dance.","expressing ability"]],"nuance":"춤 pairs with the special verb 춰요, so you say 춤을 춰요 to mean dance. The same root makes the dictionary form 춤추다.","mistakes":["Using 해요 instead of 춰요 with 춤"]},
{"kind":"noun","hangul":"그림","english":"drawing; painting","topic":"daily-life","chapterIds":["chapter-05","chapter-08"],"grammarIds":["grammar-particle-eul-reul","grammar-ending-can"],"usage":[["그림을 그려요","I draw a picture","그려요 means draw"],["그림이 예뻐요","the picture is pretty","subject marker 이"],["그림을 그릴 수 있어요","I can draw","ㄹ 수 있어요 can"],["그림 한 장","one picture","counter 장"]],"examples":[["저는 그림을 그려요.","I draw pictures.","hobby"],["이 그림이 정말 예뻐요.","This picture is really pretty.","opinion"],["저는 그림을 잘 그릴 수 있어요.","I can draw well.","expressing ability"]],"nuance":"그림 pairs with 그려요 (draw), and the two words share the same root sound. It covers both a drawing and a painting in everyday speech.","mistakes":["Using 만들어요 instead of 그려요 with 그림"]},
{"kind":"noun","hangul":"여행","english":"travel; trip","topic":"daily-life","chapterIds":["chapter-05","chapter-08"],"grammarIds":["grammar-particle-eul-reul","grammar-ending-want"],"usage":[["여행을 해요","I travel","여행해요 means travel"],["여행을 가요","I go on a trip","가요 means go"],["여행을 가고 싶어요","I want to travel","고 싶어요 want"],["여행이 즐거워요","the trip is enjoyable","subject marker 이"]],"examples":[["방학에 여행을 가요.","I go on a trip during vacation.","plan"],["저는 여행을 가고 싶어요.","I want to travel.","expressing desire"],["이번 여행이 정말 즐거워요.","This trip is really enjoyable.","opinion"]],"nuance":"여행 works with 해요 to mean travel and with 가요 to mean go on a trip. A traveler is 여행자 and a trip abroad is 해외여행.","mistakes":["Using 봐요 instead of 가요 or 해요 with 여행"]},
{"kind":"noun","hangul":"독서","english":"reading","topic":"daily-life","chapterIds":["chapter-05","chapter-08"],"grammarIds":["grammar-particle-eul-reul","grammar-particle-i-ga"],"usage":[["독서를 해요","I read","독서해요 means read"],["독서가 취미예요","reading is my hobby","subject marker 가"],["독서를 좋아해요","I like reading","좋아해요 means like"],["독서를 즐겨요","I enjoy reading","즐겨요 means enjoy"]],"examples":[["저는 밤에 독서를 해요.","I read at night.","daily habit"],["제 취미는 독서예요.","My hobby is reading.","introducing hobby"],["저는 독서를 정말 좋아해요.","I really like reading.","preference"]],"nuance":"독서 is a formal noun for reading that pairs with 해요, common in hobby talk. In casual speech people often say 책을 읽어요 instead.","mistakes":["Using 봐요 instead of 해요 with 독서"]},
{"kind":"noun","hangul":"등산","english":"hiking","topic":"daily-life","chapterIds":["chapter-05","chapter-08"],"grammarIds":["grammar-particle-eul-reul","grammar-ending-want"],"usage":[["등산을 해요","I go hiking","등산해요 means hike"],["등산을 가요","I go hiking","가요 means go"],["등산을 가고 싶어요","I want to hike","고 싶어요 want"],["등산이 힘들어요","hiking is hard","subject marker 이"]],"examples":[["주말마다 등산을 해요.","I go hiking every weekend.","habit"],["이번 주에 등산을 가고 싶어요.","I want to go hiking this week.","expressing desire"],["등산이 조금 힘들어요.","Hiking is a little hard.","opinion"]],"nuance":"등산 means climbing a mountain and pairs with 해요 or 가요. Many older Koreans enjoy 등산 as a favorite weekend hobby.","mistakes":["Using 타요 instead of 해요 or 가요 with 등산"]},
{"kind":"noun","hangul":"수영","english":"swimming","topic":"daily-life","chapterIds":["chapter-05","chapter-08"],"grammarIds":["grammar-particle-eul-reul","grammar-ending-can"],"usage":[["수영을 해요","I swim","수영해요 means swim"],["수영이 재미있어요","swimming is fun","subject marker 이"],["수영을 할 수 있어요","I can swim","ㄹ 수 있어요 can"],["수영을 배워요","I learn to swim","배워요 means learn"]],"examples":[["저는 여름에 수영을 해요.","I swim in summer.","seasonal habit"],["저는 수영을 할 수 있어요.","I can swim.","expressing ability"],["수영이 정말 재미있어요.","Swimming is really fun.","opinion"]],"nuance":"수영 pairs with 해요 to mean swim, and a swimming pool is called 수영장. Use it for the activity, not for one act of a single stroke.","mistakes":["Using 타요 instead of 해요 with 수영"]},
{"kind":"noun","hangul":"취미","english":"hobby","topic":"daily-life","chapterIds":["chapter-05","chapter-08"],"grammarIds":["grammar-particle-eul-reul","grammar-particle-i-ga"],"usage":[["취미가 뭐예요?","what is your hobby?","subject marker 가"],["취미가 있어요","I have a hobby","subject marker 가"],["취미를 즐겨요","I enjoy my hobby","즐겨요 means enjoy"],["제 취미는 운동이에요","my hobby is exercise","topic marker 는"]],"examples":[["취미가 뭐예요?","What is your hobby?","common question"],["제 취미는 영화 보기예요.","My hobby is watching movies.","introducing hobby"],["저는 취미가 많아요.","I have many hobbies.","describing"]],"nuance":"취미 is the word for a hobby and often opens small talk with 취미가 뭐예요. To name an activity hobby Koreans add 기, like 영화 보기.","mistakes":["Saying 취미를 있어요 instead of 취미가 있어요"]},
{"kind":"noun","hangul":"낚시","english":"fishing","topic":"daily-life","chapterIds":["chapter-05","chapter-08"],"grammarIds":["grammar-particle-eul-reul","grammar-ending-want"],"usage":[["낚시를 해요","I fish","낚시해요 means fish"],["낚시를 가요","I go fishing","가요 means go"],["낚시를 가고 싶어요","I want to go fishing","고 싶어요 want"],["낚시가 재미있어요","fishing is fun","subject marker 가"]],"examples":[["아버지가 낚시를 해요.","My father goes fishing.","family hobby"],["주말에 낚시를 가고 싶어요.","I want to go fishing this weekend.","expressing desire"],["낚시가 정말 재미있어요.","Fishing is really fun.","opinion"]],"nuance":"낚시 means fishing as a hobby and pairs with 해요 or 가요. The spelling has a tricky cluster, so it sounds like 낙시 when spoken.","mistakes":["Using 잡아요 alone instead of 낚시를 해요"]}]
